    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_511098f9",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two boxers in a ring, with one delivering a punch to the other. The overlaid text reads: \"when your master refuse to feed you a watermelon after you pluck cotton from his field.\" This text maps onto the visual of boxing by using the metaphor of a master-slave relationship, where the enslaved person (implied to be Black) is punished for labor (plucking cotton) by being denied food (watermelon). The phrase \"watermelon and fried chicken\" is a well-known racist stereotype that dehumanizes Black people by reducing them to food preferences and associating them with servitude. The visual of boxing, with one fighter dominating the other, reinforces the idea of racial hierarchy and violence. The meme is hateful because it uses racist imagery and language to demean a specific racial group, portraying them as inferior and deserving of punishment for labor, while also invoking a violent, degrading metaphor. The overall intent is to perpetuate harmful racial stereotypes and to mock or insult Black people through the juxtaposition of violent imagery with racist historical tropes.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d3472e4e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
